Eko Nurgoho is one of Indonesia's most provocative young[ artists] whose[ style is] a unique mix of Indonesia's rich traditions and popular[ culture] tinged with dark humor. Using a distinctive blend of high and low[ art], Nugroho' "Wayang Boc[or]"[ is] a contemporary form of theater[ in] which pupp[ets] and[ actors] weave together traditional elements of Indonesian 'wayag' (shadow pupp[ets]) with live[ theater] and scripts that cast a satiric[ view] of contemporary subjects. The show "God Bliss" tells the story of how Islam came to Java, and became absorbed[ as] part of Javanese[ culture] that includes elements of Hinduism, Buddhism, and animism. Simultaneously playful and penetrating.

